\name{cellucid_view_picture}
\alias{cellucid_view_picture}
\title{Take a picture of a view}
\usage{
cellucid_view_picture(viewer, height = 480, legend = TRUE, view, width = 640)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{height}{The plot's height in pixels. A whole number (at least 100, at most 20000). Default \code{480}, the viewer's own.}
\item{legend}{Draw the colour legend beside the plot. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{TRUE}, the viewer's own.}
\item{view}{The view: "View N" as the Compare views list numbers it; the selected view when left out. Text. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{width}{The plot's width in pixels (the picture adds its margins and the legend). A whole number (at least 100, at most 20000). Default \code{640}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{height} (The image's height in pixels), \code{notes} (What the picture leaves out of what the view shows (an overlay it cannot draw)), \code{plot} (The plot's size in the image, as asked for), \code{png} (The image, base64-encoded PNG bytes (an agent receives it as an image)), \code{view} (The view drawn, by its name), \code{width} (The image's width in pixels). Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
A PNG of a view as the figure export draws it (points, legend), returned as base64; nothing is downloaded.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{view.picture} (Views). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_view_picture(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
